@baseUrl = http://localhost:4002
@accessToken = replace-with-a-token-whose-role-has-github.manage
@githubToken = replace-with-a-github-token

### Whether issues can be filed. Anonymous: { "issuesEnabled": false }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/github

### The same route with github.manage also names the repository
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/github
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Connect a repository the token can read that has Issues enabled (204)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/github
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"repository":"owner/repository","accessToken":"{{githubToken}}"}

### A repository GitHub refuses, or without Issues: 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/github
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"repository":"owner/does-not-exist","accessToken":"{{githubToken}}"}

### Without github.manage: 401 anonymous, 403 signed in
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/github
Content-Type: application/json

{"repository":"owner/repository","accessToken":"{{githubToken}}"}

### With no GitHub:TokenEncryptionKey configured: 503

### The repository's issues, most recently updated first. 503 while nothing is connected
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/github/issues?page=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### The same list narrowed by GitHub's own search
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/github/issues?keyword=checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### One issue with its comments. A pull request number is 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/github/issues/1
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Comment as the connected token's account (201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/github/issues/1/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"body":"Thanks, this is fixed in the next release."}

### Close the issue (204)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/github/issues/1/close
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Disconnect (204). The issue routes answer 503 afterwards
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/github
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
